WEBVTT

00:00.250 --> 00:02.920
(Seiren Academy)

00:03.040 --> 00:04.210
Good morning.

00:04.290 --> 00:05.290
Good morning.

00:08.210 --> 00:10.420
Who is that girl? She's so pretty.

00:10.510 --> 00:11.590
Hey, look over there.

00:12.220 --> 00:13.970
Isn't that Kujou?

00:14.050 --> 00:15.720
We're in luck this morning.

00:17.800 --> 00:18.800
(Alisa Mikhailovna Kujou,
her father is Russian.)

00:18.800 --> 00:20.030
(First in her grade, Excels in all sports,
The student council treasurer)

00:21.980 --> 00:22.980
She's so elegant.

00:26.100 --> 00:28.610
Hey, good morning, Kujou.

00:28.690 --> 00:30.690
It's a refreshing morning, isn't it?

00:31.280 --> 00:32.690
Good morning.

00:33.990 --> 00:35.910
I don't think we've met before.

00:35.990 --> 00:37.780
I'm Ando, a second-year student.

00:38.490 --> 00:41.450
I've heard a lot about you from your sister,

00:41.540 --> 00:44.210
so I've always wanted to meet you.

00:44.920 --> 00:45.830
So?

00:45.920 --> 00:48.540
Would you like to have lunch with me?

00:48.630 --> 00:49.710
No, thank you.

00:51.760 --> 00:52.880
You're quite aloof.

00:52.970 --> 00:54.010
Well,

00:54.090 --> 00:56.720
can we at least exchange numbers?

00:57.090 --> 00:58.390
I'm sorry.

00:58.470 --> 01:00.600
I'm not interested in you.

01:05.520 --> 01:07.810
If there's nothing else, I'll get going.

01:09.860 --> 01:11.230
Also,

01:11.690 --> 01:13.740
that's against school rules.

01:16.990 --> 01:18.200
Unbelievable.

01:18.280 --> 01:21.120
Ando who is super popular among the girls
got instantly rejected.

01:21.200 --> 01:23.500
How high are her standards?

01:25.500 --> 01:26.420
It's Kujou.

01:31.500 --> 01:33.010
Good morning, Kuze.

01:37.800 --> 01:39.340
Good morning, Kuze.

01:39.430 --> 01:40.760
Did you stay up late watching anime again?

01:42.010 --> 01:43.890
Good morning, Alya.

01:43.970 --> 01:46.190
It's pretty much like that.

01:46.270 --> 01:48.270
You never learn, do you?

01:48.350 --> 01:50.940
Sacrificing sleep time
just to watch anime.

01:51.020 --> 01:53.690
You'll definitely feel sleepy
in school like this.

01:53.860 --> 01:57.820
That's true, but the anime ends at 1 a.m.

01:57.950 --> 02:00.990
I ended up talking
about my feedback for too long.

02:01.070 --> 02:02.410
Feedback?

02:03.080 --> 02:05.830
Do you mean sharing your feedback online?

02:05.950 --> 02:06.790
No.

02:06.870 --> 02:09.210
I called my otaku friends
and chatted for about two hours.

02:09.290 --> 02:10.380
Are you a fool?

02:11.790 --> 02:12.920
A fool?

02:13.300 --> 02:14.460
Maybe.

02:14.880 --> 02:19.090
If I'm a fool for expressing
my love for a piece of work

02:19.180 --> 02:20.930
regardless of time and place,

02:21.010 --> 02:23.430
then maybe I really am a fool.

02:23.510 --> 02:24.680
I'm sorry.

02:24.770 --> 02:27.100
I think you're a hopeless fool.

02:27.180 --> 02:29.770
Alya, you're looking great today.

02:33.070 --> 02:34.400
How cute.

02:36.610 --> 02:37.610
What?

02:38.110 --> 02:40.110
Did you say something?

02:40.200 --> 02:41.240
Nothing.

02:41.320 --> 02:43.870
I just said you look ugly.

02:43.950 --> 02:45.200
Well, I'm sorry.

02:45.620 --> 02:47.450
(Oral English, Geography A,
Basic Chemistry, Mathematics A, Art)

02:47.540 --> 02:48.540
What's wrong?

02:48.750 --> 02:49.830
Nothing.

02:50.710 --> 02:52.000
I'm sorry, Alya.

02:52.080 --> 02:54.250
Can I take a look
at your chemistry textbook?

02:54.340 --> 02:56.260
What's wrong? Did you forget it again?

02:56.380 --> 02:58.670
I think I left it at home.

03:00.090 --> 03:01.550
Well, I don't mind.

03:01.640 --> 03:02.680
Thank you.

03:11.400 --> 03:13.610
Iron and cobalt.

03:13.690 --> 03:16.400
Now, the next blank
should be filled with...

03:19.490 --> 03:20.820
Kuze, do you know the answer?

03:23.990 --> 03:25.450
I'm sorry.

03:27.160 --> 03:28.870
Answer it if you do.

03:29.000 --> 03:30.790
Yes.

03:31.960 --> 03:33.880
What question are we on?

03:36.800 --> 03:38.050
(2. Copper)

03:39.130 --> 03:40.260
It's number two, copper.

03:40.340 --> 03:41.510
No.

03:41.880 --> 03:43.680
Kujou, answer it for him.

03:43.760 --> 03:44.640
Yes.

03:45.760 --> 03:47.310
The answer is number eight, nickel.

03:47.390 --> 03:48.310
That's right.

03:48.680 --> 03:51.310
Kuze, pay attention in class.

03:53.440 --> 03:54.400
Okay.

03:55.560 --> 03:58.030
Don't tell me the wrong answer
without batting an eye.

03:58.110 --> 04:01.110
I'm just telling you
what question we're on.

04:01.900 --> 04:05.200
You were clearly pointing at number two.

04:05.660 --> 04:07.410
That's an awful accusation.

04:09.290 --> 04:10.910
Your eyes are smiling.

04:11.000 --> 04:12.460
How cute.

04:15.080 --> 04:15.960
What did you say?

04:16.460 --> 04:18.590
I said you're a fool.

04:22.800 --> 04:24.300
How cute.

04:25.050 --> 04:26.930
How cute.

04:27.010 --> 04:29.930
Why do you say I'm cute?
What exactly do you mean?

04:30.020 --> 04:31.680
You said the same thing just now.

04:31.770 --> 04:35.020
I understood all of that, you know?

04:36.060 --> 04:39.190
You're blushing like a baby.

04:41.110 --> 04:43.610
Who's the baby here?

06:05.530 --> 06:07.530
(Alya Sometimes Hides Her Feelings in Russian)

06:15.500 --> 06:16.370
When I was in elementary school,

06:16.370 --> 06:17.290
(Episode 1: Alya Hides Her Feelings in Russian)
When I was in elementary school,

06:17.370 --> 06:20.800
(Episode 1: Alya Hides Her Feelings in Russian)
I used to play with a Russian girl
who lived near my grandpa's house.

06:20.800 --> 06:21.710
I used to play with a Russian girl
who lived near my grandpa's house.

06:22.380 --> 06:24.380
I think I learned it over time.

06:24.760 --> 06:27.970
Even now, I can still understand
most of the Russian language.

06:28.840 --> 06:30.050
It's just that

06:30.140 --> 06:32.180
I didn't expect to meet someone like her.

06:32.680 --> 06:35.520
The Russian beauty who sits next to me

06:35.600 --> 06:39.560
only uses Russian to hide her feelings.

06:40.480 --> 06:43.400
If I were to tell her now
that I understood everything...

06:48.450 --> 06:49.820
I can't bring myself to say it.

06:56.080 --> 06:59.000
Except in emergencies
and for educational purposes,

06:59.080 --> 07:01.750
it's against school rules
to use a mobile phone in school.

07:01.830 --> 07:04.380
Then I didn't break any school rules.

07:04.460 --> 07:05.840
Because this is an emergency.

07:06.340 --> 07:07.970
Just asking.

07:08.050 --> 07:09.300
How is this an emergency?

07:09.380 --> 07:10.550
Because in 10 minutes,

07:10.630 --> 07:12.050
the free card draw will be over.

07:13.720 --> 07:16.810
How dare you say that in front
of a member of the student council?

07:17.220 --> 07:20.440
The SSR Tsukuyomi is here!

07:20.520 --> 07:21.600
Confiscated!

07:21.690 --> 07:22.560
No.

07:23.520 --> 07:24.730
"Tsukuyomi"?

07:24.820 --> 07:28.110
Tsukuyomi is the moon god
in Japanese mythology, right?

07:28.490 --> 07:30.820
Why does she have silver hair
instead of black?

07:31.110 --> 07:31.990
Who knows?

07:32.070 --> 07:33.820
Maybe it's to match the moon.

07:33.910 --> 07:35.410
Don't worry about the details.

07:35.490 --> 07:36.740
She's cute after all.

07:38.580 --> 07:40.620
Thank you for understanding.

07:42.000 --> 07:44.250
It's really Lord Tsukuyomi.

07:45.500 --> 07:50.720
I'm also silver-haired, you playboy.

07:52.130 --> 07:53.800
What did you say?

07:53.890 --> 07:56.310
I said you are a game loser.

07:57.810 --> 08:00.390
Hey, that's rude.

08:00.480 --> 08:01.850
W-What?

08:01.940 --> 08:05.480
You called me,
who is a non-paying user, a loser.

08:05.940 --> 08:09.690
Don't you think it's rude to those users
who spend heavily on games?

08:12.530 --> 08:13.360
You're right.

08:13.450 --> 08:16.370
I don't think anyone wants
to be compared to you.

08:16.450 --> 08:17.620
That's harsh.

08:19.290 --> 08:22.120
You look so serious.
I thought you'd say something important.

08:22.210 --> 08:24.000
Hey, I didn't expect you to say that.

08:24.080 --> 08:27.040
It's not an exaggeration
to say that's my strength.

08:27.290 --> 08:29.630
That's the biggest lie of the century.

08:30.210 --> 08:32.760
There's still 80 percent
of the century left.

08:33.760 --> 08:35.550
(Ordering Counter) (Tray Return)

08:37.390 --> 08:38.810
I want to be popular!

08:40.220 --> 08:42.480
Masachika, what are you eating?

08:42.560 --> 08:43.850
Extra spicy mapo ramen.

08:43.940 --> 08:46.020
Hey, don't ignore me.

08:47.480 --> 08:49.110
I thought it was just a symptom.

08:49.190 --> 08:51.400
This is why I hate popular guys.

08:52.490 --> 08:54.660
(Pick-up Counter)
Hey, they're the members of the student council.

08:55.110 --> 08:56.660
(Alisa Mikhailovna Kujou)
I guess we're too late.

08:56.740 --> 08:58.370
(The student council treasurer)
I wonder if there are any seats left.

08:58.830 --> 09:00.620
(Maria Mikhailovna Kujou)
It's okay.

09:00.620 --> 09:04.250
(The student council secretary)
I'll just eat with my classmates over there.

09:04.330 --> 09:07.880
(Yuki Suou)
Masha, thank you for understanding.

09:07.880 --> 09:08.880
(The student council public relations)

09:08.880 --> 09:10.840
Kujou and the others

09:10.920 --> 09:12.300
are really beautiful.

09:12.380 --> 09:14.930
Kujou is stunning.

09:15.010 --> 09:17.050
I really want to get to know her.

09:17.140 --> 09:20.510
But it seems like Kujou has a boyfriend.

09:21.560 --> 09:23.600
Apparently, every guy who confessed to her

09:23.680 --> 09:27.060
was turned down with the excuse
that she already had a boyfriend.

09:27.400 --> 09:30.400
Even if she doesn't have a boyfriend,
Takeshi doesn't stand a chance.

09:30.480 --> 09:31.530
Shut up!

09:31.610 --> 09:34.650
Don't get cocky just because
you're friends with Princess Alya.

09:35.780 --> 09:37.240
I'm so jealous.

09:37.320 --> 09:38.950
I can't believe

09:39.030 --> 09:42.080
you were allowed to address
that aloof princess with a nickname.

09:42.490 --> 09:43.750
Not really.

09:45.500 --> 09:47.620
All I do is annoy her all the time.

09:48.040 --> 09:50.290
It's still better
than being treated indifferently.

09:50.380 --> 09:53.050
Princess Alya doesn't talk
to anyone anyway.

09:53.710 --> 09:57.180
We've been sitting
next to each other for over a year.

09:57.260 --> 09:59.510
If I were to choose someone
to approach among them,

09:59.600 --> 10:01.180
Suou seems like the better option.

10:01.430 --> 10:02.600
She's more approachable.

10:02.680 --> 10:05.520
Compared to Princess Alya, there seems
to be a better chance to get close to her,

10:05.600 --> 10:08.600
even though she's still out of my league.

10:08.900 --> 10:10.770
Do you think there's any chance?

10:10.860 --> 10:12.860
But it seems like
she has rejected confessions

10:12.940 --> 10:14.440
more times than Kujou.

10:14.530 --> 10:17.150
You're right.

10:17.240 --> 10:20.280
Could it be that she has a fiance
like the other girls?

10:20.370 --> 10:22.020
Masachika, any news from your end?

10:22.490 --> 10:23.830
Why are you asking me?

10:23.950 --> 10:25.410
Because you...

10:37.380 --> 10:41.090
Masachika, can we sit here?

10:42.600 --> 10:45.060
Well, I don't mind.

10:45.140 --> 10:46.600
You guys are fine too, right?

10:48.690 --> 10:49.600
Please have a seat.

10:49.690 --> 10:51.190
Thank you.

10:52.900 --> 10:56.400
Masachika, you ordered
the same thing, didn't you?

10:56.490 --> 11:00.030
I didn't know you ate
that kind of food, Suou.

11:00.110 --> 11:02.910
You don't have to be so formal.

11:02.990 --> 11:04.540
We're in the same grade after all.

11:04.620 --> 11:06.790
Well, okay.

11:07.250 --> 11:08.120
Besides,

11:08.210 --> 11:10.710
I still eat ramen

11:10.790 --> 11:13.790
and I often go out to eat on weekends.

11:22.890 --> 11:24.430
It's delicious,

11:24.510 --> 11:27.390
but I feel like it could be spicier.

11:27.470 --> 11:28.390
Right?

11:28.520 --> 11:30.480
If only we had some chili oil.

11:31.770 --> 11:33.650
Maybe we can bring it up

11:33.730 --> 11:35.820
at the next student council meeting.

11:36.020 --> 11:38.690
Wait, how could you mix
public and personal matters?

11:38.780 --> 11:39.860
I'm just kidding.

11:42.200 --> 11:44.200
Are you two close?

11:44.700 --> 11:47.490
We're childhood friends.

11:47.580 --> 11:49.120
Childhood friends?

11:49.250 --> 11:50.080
Yes.

11:50.160 --> 11:52.920
We've been going to the same school
since kindergarten.

11:53.460 --> 11:54.840
I see.

11:55.380 --> 11:57.880
By the way, are you two close?

11:57.960 --> 12:01.720
We're just getting to know each other.

12:01.800 --> 12:06.890
At the very least,
I want to be friends with Alisa.

12:08.180 --> 12:09.810
Even if you become friends with me,

12:09.890 --> 12:11.560
I don't think you'll find it fun.

12:12.560 --> 12:13.600
In other words,

12:13.690 --> 12:18.280
you don't mind
being friends with me, right?

12:20.190 --> 12:22.400
Well, I guess so.

12:23.030 --> 12:25.780
Well, we're done eating.

12:26.530 --> 12:27.580
Please excuse us.

12:29.450 --> 12:32.330
It's a little too bright here,
so I can't stand it.

12:36.130 --> 12:37.170
By the way,

12:39.420 --> 12:40.590
Masachika,

12:40.670 --> 12:44.300
have you thought about the offer
to join the student council?

12:44.380 --> 12:45.890
I've told you many times.

12:45.970 --> 12:47.550
I have no intention of joining it.

12:47.850 --> 12:49.010
If you join the council,

12:49.100 --> 12:52.310
you should be able
to work well with me and Alisa.

12:52.390 --> 12:53.310
After all,

12:53.390 --> 12:55.980
you were the vice president
of the student council.

12:57.190 --> 12:58.820
In the middle school student council,

12:58.900 --> 13:00.230
I was the president

13:00.320 --> 13:02.400
and Masachika was the vice president.

13:02.900 --> 13:04.400
I see.

13:04.860 --> 13:07.240
I was only joining
because Yuki asked me to.

13:07.320 --> 13:09.120
In our school's student council election,

13:09.200 --> 13:11.410
the president and vice president
had to team up,

13:11.500 --> 13:13.500
so I had no choice but to help.

13:14.830 --> 13:18.210
This might come
as a bit of a surprise to you.

13:18.290 --> 13:21.760
Masachika may not look like it,
but he's serious when he needs to be.

13:22.380 --> 13:24.010
What do you mean by that?

13:25.130 --> 13:26.050
Who knows?

13:26.130 --> 13:28.550
I've known about that for a long time.

13:31.520 --> 13:32.520
(Red bean soup)

13:35.520 --> 13:36.850
You guys get along so well.

13:36.940 --> 13:38.020
Surprised?

13:38.110 --> 13:39.520
Yes, I'm surprised.

13:39.610 --> 13:42.360
I didn't expect you
to have a female friend.

13:42.440 --> 13:43.780
Is that why you're surprised?

13:44.900 --> 13:45.900
What?

13:45.990 --> 13:47.490
Well, because...

13:48.410 --> 13:49.700
You're my female friend too.

13:51.410 --> 13:53.750
Are we friends?

13:53.870 --> 13:55.370
What? Aren't we?

13:56.330 --> 13:59.290
You're right. We are friends.

13:59.790 --> 14:01.800
Hey, where are you going?

14:01.880 --> 14:05.300
I just remembered I have to go
to the student council room.

14:06.800 --> 14:08.180
What's that all about?

14:18.980 --> 14:20.150
Hey!

14:21.400 --> 14:22.860
Maschaka.

14:23.280 --> 14:25.900
I told you, it's "Masachika."

14:26.320 --> 14:26.830
Hahaha.

14:27.780 --> 14:30.910
Come up here, Maschaka.

14:35.250 --> 14:37.500
Look, it's the sunset.

14:37.580 --> 14:38.710
Right.

14:38.790 --> 14:40.750
It's "beauty"?

14:40.830 --> 14:42.090
It's "beautiful."

14:42.170 --> 14:43.500
It's beautiful.

14:54.390 --> 14:57.230
See you tomorrow, Maschaka.

14:57.310 --> 14:58.480
See you tomorrow.

15:08.200 --> 15:10.530
I studied Russian

15:10.610 --> 15:13.450
because I wanted to talk to her so badly.

15:14.620 --> 15:15.620
But now,

15:15.700 --> 15:17.200
I don't even remember her name.

15:20.710 --> 15:22.920
Good morning.

15:23.040 --> 15:25.210
(Students on duty: Kujou, Kuze)

15:36.600 --> 15:39.310
I did a good job.

15:41.810 --> 15:43.110
Hey, good morning.

15:43.610 --> 15:45.400
Good morning, Kuze.

15:45.770 --> 15:48.070
I woke up early today.

15:48.610 --> 15:51.200
I have nothing to do anyway,
so I got some work done.

15:51.610 --> 15:53.660
Kuze, you're up early.

15:53.870 --> 15:55.950
Is it going to snow today?

15:56.030 --> 15:57.120
Alya.

15:57.200 --> 15:59.330
Your Japanese is really good.

16:01.210 --> 16:03.790
I'll clean the blackboard in the morning.

16:03.880 --> 16:05.290
Thank you.

16:06.800 --> 16:08.130
What happened to your socks?

16:08.210 --> 16:10.300
Did you step in a puddle?

16:10.420 --> 16:13.510
No, I'm not like you.

16:13.590 --> 16:16.390
Who are you calling absent-minded?

16:18.470 --> 16:20.480
I didn't go that far.

16:21.230 --> 16:23.730
They got wet from the splash
caused by a passing truck.

16:24.610 --> 16:26.190
That was a disaster.

16:26.480 --> 16:27.320
Well,

16:27.400 --> 16:30.690
it's my fault for walking
too close to the road.

16:31.320 --> 16:33.030
I have spare socks,

16:33.110 --> 16:34.110
so it's okay.

16:36.200 --> 16:37.120
Kuze.

16:37.990 --> 16:40.000
When you and Suou were in middle school,

16:40.080 --> 16:42.580
you both were
student council committees, right?

16:43.420 --> 16:44.710
Yes, we were.

16:48.300 --> 16:49.590
Hey, Kuze.

16:50.340 --> 16:52.630
Are you really not going to join
the student council?

16:52.720 --> 16:54.720
Why are you even asking too?

16:54.800 --> 16:55.890
Answer me.

16:57.100 --> 17:00.270
Yes, I'm not going
to join the student council.

17:01.310 --> 17:03.600
What if I...

17:05.100 --> 17:06.980
Never mind. It's nothing.

17:23.870 --> 17:24.920
Hey.

17:25.000 --> 17:28.340
Can you get me spare socks from my locker?

17:29.590 --> 17:31.170
I've already taken off my socks.

17:31.260 --> 17:32.710
I can't walk there to get them.

17:33.130 --> 17:35.260
Hurry up.

17:36.800 --> 17:38.050
All right.

17:40.430 --> 17:41.600
I'm opening it.

17:45.270 --> 17:46.190
Here you go.

17:46.520 --> 17:47.860
Help me put it on.

17:48.610 --> 17:49.520
What's wrong?

17:49.610 --> 17:51.280
You're asking me what's wrong?

17:51.360 --> 17:53.030
I should be the one asking you that.

17:53.110 --> 17:55.320
This is to thank you for getting my socks.

17:55.400 --> 17:57.660
It's a reward for you, right?

17:58.030 --> 18:00.990
No, only a minority of the special group
consider it a reward.

18:01.080 --> 18:02.450
So it's not?

18:02.540 --> 18:03.910
No, it's a reward.

18:04.620 --> 18:06.670
It's a reward for me too.

18:08.250 --> 18:09.920
I've always thought so.

18:10.000 --> 18:12.920
Why does she use Russian
to hide her feelings?

18:13.010 --> 18:16.010
Is it because she's a perfectionist

18:16.090 --> 18:18.550
that she has been stressed out
to become her ideal self?

18:18.800 --> 18:22.100
Maybe this is her way
of venting her stress?

18:22.180 --> 18:24.430
In other words, mental exposure.

18:24.520 --> 18:26.190
Is she an exhibitionist?

18:26.690 --> 18:27.520
What?

18:27.600 --> 18:28.520
Nothing.

18:28.940 --> 18:30.690
I was just thinking about what you said.

18:31.320 --> 18:32.520
Nothing.

18:32.610 --> 18:34.690
I said you're a wimp.

18:34.780 --> 18:37.950
Forget it. I'll put them on myself.

18:38.410 --> 18:40.240
No, there's no need.

